      ]
    },
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "Say the pronoun, then the verb with the ending for the person: <em>Je parle français. Tu travailles ici ? Nous habitons à Lille.</em>",
        "tag": "The ending"
      },
      {
        "html": "Many endings are <strong>silent</strong>: <em>parle, parles, parlent</em> sound the same. Only <em>nous</em> (<em>-ons</em>) and <em>vous</em> (<em>-ez</em>) sound different. In writing you must still add the right ending.",
        "tag": "Silent endings"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>je</strong> becomes <strong>j'</strong> before a vowel or a mute h: <em>j'habite, j'aime, j'arrive, j'étudie</em>. Before a consonant it stays: <em>je parle, je travaille, je mange</em>.",
        "tag": "je or j'"
      },
      {
        "html": "The present is for what happens <strong>now</strong>, for <strong>habits</strong> and for <strong>facts</strong>. It also means “I am working”: <em>Aujourd'hui, je travaille à la maison. Le lundi, je mange chez ma mère. J'habite à Nantes.</em>",
        "tag": "When"
      },
      {
        "html": "Two ways to ask: <em>Tu parles anglais ?</em> (rising voice) or <em>Est-ce que tu parles anglais ?</em> Both use the normal verb form.",
        "tag": "Questions"
      },
      {
        "html": "Spelling note: with <em>nous</em>, <em>manger</em> keeps its <em>e</em> and <em>commencer</em> takes <em>ç</em>, to keep the sound: <em>nous mangeons, nous commençons</em>.",
        "tag": "Spelling"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Common mistakes: ✗ <em>Je parler français</em> → ✓ <em>Je parle français</em>. ✗ <em>Elle habites ici</em> → ✓ <em>Elle habite ici</em>. ✗ <em>Je habite à Paris</em> → ✓ <em>J'habite à Paris</em>. Next: <a href=\"/etre-avoir\">être and avoir</a> and <a href=\"/present-irreguliers\">key irregular verbs</a>.",
    "reference": {
      "showLabel": "Show overview ▼",
      "hideLabel": "Hide overview ▲",
